<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Andrés Malong</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. <a href="/years/1661">1661</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/17th-century">17th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Andrés Malong was a Pangasinan chief from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/san-carlos-pangasinan">Binalatongan</a> who led a revolt against Spanish rule in 1660–1661. Proclaimed king of Pangasinan by his followers, he sought to spread the uprising to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilocos">Ilocos</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pampanga">Pampanga</a>, but Spanish forces sent by Governor-General Manrique de Lara defeated him, and he was executed in 1661.</p></div>
